You are tasked with implementing a program that simulates a simple task scheduler. The program should be able to add tasks with different priorities and execute them based on their priority. 

You are given a code snippet for a `TaskScheduler` class with a `Start` method that currently does nothing. Your task is to complete the `TaskScheduler` class by implementing the following methods:
- `AddTask(string taskName, int priority)`: Adds a new task with the given name and priority to the scheduler.
- `ExecuteNextTask()`: Executes the task with the highest priority and removes it from the scheduler. If multiple tasks have the same highest priority, execute the one that was added first.
- `GetAllTasks()`: Returns a list of all tasks in the scheduler, sorted by priority (highest priority first). If multiple tasks have the same priority, maintain the order in which they were added.

You should implement the `Task` class to represent a task with a name and priority.

Your task is to complete the `TaskScheduler` class and the `Task` class to meet the requirements.

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.PriorityQueue;

public class TaskScheduler {
    private PriorityQueue<Task> taskQueue;

    public TaskScheduler() {
        taskQueue = new PriorityQueue<>();
    }

    public void AddTask(String taskName, int priority) {
        taskQueue.add(new Task(taskName, priority));
    }

    public void ExecuteNextTask() {
        if (!taskQueue.isEmpty()) {
            Task nextTask = taskQueue.poll();
            System.out.println("Executing task: " + nextTask.getName());
        } else {
            System.out.println("No tasks to execute.");
        }
    }

    public List<Task> GetAllTasks() {
        List<Task> allTasks = new ArrayList<>(taskQueue);
        allTasks.sort((t1, t2) -> {
            if (t1.getPriority() != t2.getPriority()) {
                return Integer.compare(t2.getPriority(), t1.getPriority());
            } else {
                return Integer.compare(taskQueue.indexOf(t1), taskQueue.indexOf(t2));
            }
        });
        return allTasks;
    }

    private class Task implements Comparable<Task> {
        private String name;
        private int priority;

        public Task(String name, int priority) {
            this.name = name;
            this.priority = priority;
        }

        public String getName() {
            return name;
        }

        public int getPriority() {
            return priority;
        }

        @Override
        public int compareTo(Task other) {
            if (this.priority != other.priority) {
                return Integer.compare(other.priority, this.priority);
            } else {
                return Integer.compare(taskQueue.indexOf(this), taskQueue.indexOf(other));
            }
        }
    }
}
